#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:9
msgid "Single Particle Model (SPM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:21
msgid "Model Equations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:32
msgid ""
"The SPM consists of two spherically symmetric diffusion equations: one "
"within a representative negative particle (:math:`\\text{k}=\\text{n}`) and "
"one within a representative positive particle (:math:`\\text{k}=\\text{p}`). "
"In the centre of the particle the standard no-flux condition is imposed. "
"Since the SPM assumes that all particles in an electrode behave in exactly "
"the same way, the flux on the surface of a particle is simply the current :"
"math:`I` divided by the thickness of the electrode :math:`L_{\\text{k}}`. "
"The concentration of lithium in electrode :math:`\\text{k}` is denoted :math:"
"`c_{\\text{k}}` and the current is denoted by :math:`I`. The model equations "
"for the SPM are then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:35
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\partial c_{\\text{s,k}}}{\\partial t} = -\\frac{1}{r_{\\text{k}}^2} "
"\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial r_{\\text{k}}} \\left(r_{\\text{k}}^2 "
"N_{\\text{s,k}}\\right), \\\\\n"
"N_{\\text{s,k}} = -D_{\\text{s,k}}(c_{\\text{s,k}}) \\frac{\\partial "
"c_{\\text{s,k}}}{\\partial r_{\\text{k}}}, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, "
"p},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:41
msgid ""
"N_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=0} = 0, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, "
"p}, \\quad \\ \\ - N_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=1} =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"          \\frac{I}{Fa_{\\text{n}}L_{\\text{n}}}, \\quad &\\text{k}"
"=\\text{n}, \\\\\n"
"          -\\frac{I}{Fa_{\\text{p}}L_{\\text{p}}}, \\quad &\\text{k}"
"=\\text{p},\n"
"\\end{cases} \\\\\n"
"c_{\\text{s,k}}(r_{\\text{k}},0) = c_{\\text{s,k,0}}, \\quad \\text{k} \\in "
"\\text{n, p},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:51
msgid ""
"where :math:`D_{\\text{s,k}}` is the diffusion coefficient in the solid, :"
"math:`N_{\\text{s,k}}` denotes the flux of lithium ions in the solid "
"particle within the region :math:`\\text{k}`, and :math:`r_{\\text{k}} "
"\\in[0,1]` is the radial coordinate of the particle in electrode :math:"
"`\\text{k}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:54
msgid "Voltage Expression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:56
msgid "The voltage is obtained from the expression:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:58
msgid ""
"V = U_{\\text{p}}(c_{\\text{p}})\\big|_{r_{\\text{p}}=1} - U_{\\text{n}}"
"(c_{\\text{n}})\\big|_{r_{\\text{n}}=1} - \\frac{2RT}"
"{F}\\sinh^{-1}\\left(\\frac{I}{2j_{\\text{0,p}} a_{\\text{p}}"
"L_{\\text{p}}}\\right) - \\frac{2RT}{F}\\sinh^{-1}\\left(\\frac{I}"
"{2j_{\\text{0,n}} a_{\\text{p}}L_{\\text{n}}}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:63
msgid "with the exchange current densities given by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb:65
msgid ""
"j_{\\text{0,k}} =  (c_{\\text{k}})^{1/2}(1-c_{\\text{k}})^{1/2}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

